# Keep host build output out of the image context.
#
# Both Dockerfiles restore from the .csproj alone (for layer caching) and then COPY the
# project directory over it with --no-restore to follow. If the host has ever built these
# projects locally, that second COPY drops a host obj/project.assets.json -- full of
# /home/<user>/.nuget paths that do not exist in the container -- on top of the container's
# own restore, and publish fails with NETSDK1064 "package ... was not found". It looks like
# a missing package; it is a leaked assets file.
#
# This became reachable the moment the repo grew a local dev shell with a .NET SDK in it.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Not build inputs.
runs/
.tools/
tests/fixtures/
.git/
